{"text": "Office of the New York State Comptroller\nThomas P DiNapoli * State Comptroller\n\nFiscal Stress Monitoring System*\n\nThe Fiscal Stress Monitoring System and resulting fiscal stress designations rely on data (as of 12/31/2018)\nfrom ST-3 reports submitted by school districts to the State Education Department.\n\nThis list (Sorted in order of fiscal stress score) reflects a fiscal year end date of June 30, 2018.\n\nSchool district information for the fiscally dependent districts (Buffalo, Rochester, Syracuse and Yonkers)\nwill be incorporated into the scoring of their respective cities.\n\nSi ant Stress\nGreater than or equal to 65% of total points\n\nName County Economic Development Fiscal\nRegion Score\n\nEldred Central School District Sullivan Mid-Hudson Region 73.3\nNew Suffolk Common School District Suffolk Long Island 70.0\nNorwich City School District Chenango Southern Tier 70.0\nSchenevus Central School District Otsego Southern Tier 66.7\n\nWyandanch Union Free School District Suffolk Long Island 65.0\n\nModerate Stress\nGreater than or equal to 45% of total points\n\nNo school districts meet criteria for Moderate Fiscal Stress classification.\nIf a school district is not shown on this list, it may not have filed its ST-3 report,\n\nmay have data that is inconclusive for FSMS or may have no designation.\n\nLearn more about the System and Scoring\n\nDivision of Local Government and School Accountability",
